Z||000000||fiero56||01-19-2001||09:36 PM||||I was sitting in my economics class today(bored as usual), and decided I would make up a little sheet detailing how much it actually costs me in wear and tear to drive my Fiero one mile. the project mushroomed to more than 31 items on my list that I know mileage intervals for, but have others that I am unsure if I should incluce. I am going to list different parts here, and need to know if they are considered parts that have a usual life span. If anyone could give me an approximate mileage life-span for any of these parts post it here. Or, if these parts don't have a typical life span, post that here too. Thanks.<P>tie-rod ends<BR>suspension bushings<BR>coolant hoses<BR>cables(throttle, shift, select, parking brake, etc)<BR>clutch set<BR>radiator<BR>heater core<BR>brake calipers<BR>brake pads<BR>brake lines<BR>brake rotors<BR>brake master cylinder<BR>wheel bearings<BR>shocks<BR>struts<BR>alignment<BR>clutch m.c & s.c.<BR>CAT<P>any more? Thanks for all help. I will post my findings after this is finished.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 01-19-2001).]||||reg||2
