Z||000006||theogre||01-20-2001||08:06 PM||||How long the cooling system parts last is directly liked to coolant condition. All traditional coolants have a finite life span. About 2 years. Even traditional coolant that is in sealed retail packaging will deteriorate over time. <P>Life of cooling system parts can also be shortend by vehicle storage. Left sitting, the components of the coolant separate. This leaves plain water at the top of the system. The water will corode cooling system parts, usually at the line where the water and any trapped air meet.<P>On the O2 sensor, the jury is out on that one. Even Bosch, the leading maker of them, doesn't have a definative answer. One big reason is O2 sensor life is effected by a large number of things. In a properly running engine the thing can last years. If it gets contaminated it can be dead in seconds depending on the contaminant. Don't forget.... you can contaminate the outside of this sensor as easily as the inside.||||reg||1
Z||000007||fiero56||01-21-2001||08:00 PM||||Back to top.||||reg||1
Z||000008||fiero56||01-22-2001||01:42 PM||||Last time I bumping this to top. If no replies with mileage intervals or such, I will leave these items out of my calculations.||||reg||1
Z||000009||286SE'S||01-24-2001||11:32 AM||||The only thing I can see on your list that you know that you will be changing at about<BR>30,000 miles is those brake pads. I know they are not expensive but should be considerd as<BR>a known wear item. The other stuff? You don't know how long they will last. So much depends on proper lubrication, coolant changes, driving conditions, rough roads and the driver himself. Some mechanical things will last a long time if the car is not driven much (low mileage) Others will just go bad from time and exposure to the elements like dew wipes, seat upholstery and paint.<BR>I think shocks and struts are a time item. After 12-16 years they just lose their seals.<BR>I was suprized when my heater core failed at about 102,000 but since it is a cheap and easy to replace item,(since you are changing the coolant anyway) I did not set money aside for its eventual demise.<BR>I think if I ever wrote down how much my Fieros cost me, I would be unhappy with the<BR>amount but knowing people with $300 a month car payments on top of Gas, Oil, Insurance, ect... I would still not want a new car.||||reg||1
